{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire","id":968857,"title":"The Syndicate and the Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T17:41:06-07:00","id":968857,"title":"The Syndicate and the Vampire","content":"I have always wondered why the Syndicate has not already bankrupted every single Vampire through Entropic Effects, Enlightened management and hypereconomics manipulations. why the most competitive and ruthless of the Conventions(though not necessarily greedy), has left their immortal (potential) financial rivals and (also potential) business competitors largely intact so long like ancient, festering tumor, especially in the Mage-centric setting. What is your thought regarding the reason? Do you have any theory or conjecture?<br /> <br /> To me, the most plausible answer is simply &quot;Vampire is more popular than Mage&quot;. I could not find other, more probable reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:56:20-07:00","id":968868,"title":"","content":"Probably because the projected market correction (paradox) from said actions is well out of tolerable levels. You are dealing in some cases with creatures that have been in the finance and markets since they frist became a thing. To try and remove them would do more harm then good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:13:34-07:00","id":968876,"title":"","content":"Some of them probably created the first financial markets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:18:21-07:00","id":968880,"title":"","content":"Isn't there already a technocrat vs vampire thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:23:04-07:00","id":968883,"title":"","content":"Because for the most part, vampires don't have money. Vampire pawns have money and if you financially ruin them, the loss spreads to Syndicate interests as well and then the vampires just find new pawns. It would inconvenience the vampires, yes, but it would probably hurt the Syndicate more. Vampires amassing wealth doesn't really hurt the Syndicate either unless the vampires use their wealth against them, which is they seldom would. Also, vampires can be really dangerous and so it would be best not to piss them off unless you had a lot to gain by doing so and the Syndicate doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:26:49-07:00","id":968887,"title":"","content":"Besides, why should you try to ruin your incredibly powerful and influential competitors who would most likely make any attempt at doing so a Pyrrhic Victory at best, when teaming up with them in order to spread your influence through their lines is far less ruinous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:33:13-07:00","id":968894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=968887#post968887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, why should you try to ruin your incredibly powerful and influential competitors who would most likely make any attempt at doing so a Pyrrhic Victory at best, when teaming up with them in order to spread your influence through their lines is far less ruinous?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that the Syndicate and vampires already do team up even if neither are completely aware of it. Large scale financial control likely involves huge multinational corporations which are often closely tied together as well as banks and other monetary institutions. Any big money organization like that is likely full of both vampire and Syndicate influence and so both groups profit together. Maybe the Syndicate could try to limit vampiric influence within their companies, but then you also limit the ways in which vampires use their powers and influence to bolster those companies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:40:53-07:00","id":968902,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla, which would be the most likely vampire group to deal with the Syndicate on an equal footing, is almost as wealthy as the Syndicate. Their elders are also capable of superhuman intelligence without suffering permanent Paradox and are capable of frighteningly high orders of social engineering that the Syndicate really cannot counter without involving the Oracles (who honestly cannot return to the Earth without exploding because of their accumulated permanent Paradox and that is if they survived the Avatar Storm). The Camarilla is also interested in keeping the supernatural a secret, the Masquerade, so the Syndicate is willing to turn a blind eye to their activities as long as the Camarilla does not start undermining the work of the Syndicate. Anyway, the Syndicate has more pressing concerns, like dealing with those damn Virtual Adepts who keep promoting bitcoins and other virtual currencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T23:58:16-07:00","id":969058,"title":"","content":"It is certain that the Syndicate would target and obliterate the Giovanni if they know their presence...but then again, I bet the Technocracy don't aware, or even heard of existence of this particular Necromancer Clan, and for that matter, any other Independent Clans, with possible exception of NWO. So the Vampire groups Syndics would be most likely privy are the Camarilla and the Sabbat, and unlike Camarilla, Sabbat's power is not derived from money, subtle influence and canny machinations, but terror, brute force and wanton excesses. And I do agree with Sergeant Brother's opinion mostly - the Syndicate and the Camarilla are allies and helping each other, and not in just global, but local scale as well, whether they are aware it or not.<br /> <br /> In fact, I can easily imagine New York Syndics and Camarilla are routinely making deal for mutual benefits, systemically finding, ruining and suborning what puny sources of funding Sabbat might clasp in its paw while taking care to avoid trespassing others' businesses, and more than a few of them are fast, long-time friends or friendly rivals respecting each other at the very least. Their interests do not collide. Their purpose does not in conflict. It is actually on the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-14-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:53:13-07:00","id":969077,"title":"","content":"Yes, as long as Camarilla vampires avoid Technocracy personnel and visa versa, I think that everyone is willing to live and let live, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T03:51:20-07:00","id":969127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969077#post969077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, as long as Camarilla vampires avoid Technocracy personnel and visa versa, I think that everyone is willing to live and let live, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think the Technocracy as a whole is not running into many conflicts with the Camarilla, as the Camarilla *itself* is highly invested in not revealing its existance to the human population - which serves the Technocracy just perfectly fine along the lines of &quot;You don't cause a mess, we won't need to clean it up. As you were.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:26:19-07:00","id":969136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=968868#post968868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably because the projected market correction (paradox) from said actions is well out of tolerable levels. You are dealing in some cases with creatures that have been in the finance and markets since they frist became a thing. To try and remove them would do more harm then good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, and remember that the financial market is the weak point of the Syndicate.<br /> A lot of hyper-fast financial transaction are mumbo-jumbo highly paradoxical procedures, and they are risky, very risky.<br /> The Syndicate and the Technocracy can be hurt by financial crisis, there is a reason if NWO is so pissed about the last economic cycle, and even more important the Syndicate can't protect the Financial Market as they can protect other sectors of the economy.<br /> <br /> Remember the the Technocracy in Asia was almost economically wiped out at the time of the 1997 asian financial crisis,and they were hit hard by the crisis in 2008 and 2010.<br /> And all these crisis where caused by &quot;outside influence&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The truth of the Flash Crash is still uncertain. The algorithm that caused it did so with such lethal precision that there\u2019s <b>no question it was a concerted attack.<br /> Theories abound; terrorist action by the Virtual Adepts, an artificial intelligence gone rogue or something else yet unknown.</b> <b>What is certain is that despite the Syndicate\u2019s best efforts, the stock market represents a dangerously under-defended system.</b> For now, executives man the walls and keep watch, in case whoever caused the Crash makes another attempt.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> even more the NWO is quite sure that the Greece was broke by a group of &quot;Vampire necromancers&quot; (Giovanni?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flash forward to a few years later. During a rash of scandals relating to the world\u2019s economic crisis,<b> some information surfaced that implicated vampiric necromancers in the Greek financial collapse.</b> This information made national news. While it didn\u2019t mention vampires by name, it did mention shell companies and family names that could easily be traced back by an enterprising journalist. The Order decided it needed a media task force to keep this from happening again. It brought Jones on to act as Control for this amalgam, and hired Vo to form and lead the group. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The crisis in 2007 in America was started by vampire anarchs to hit the Camarilla elders<br /> <br /> Anarchs unbond<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As intended, the disproportionate reaction led to widespread sympathy for the Anarch cause from younger Kindred offended by the response. Then, when the Camarilla\u2019s suppression campaign was at its height, the Red Question sprang its trap. On August 8, 2007, a terse message arrived electronically to each of the Camarilla Justicars via untraceable means: \u201cWe have noted your<br /> response to our pursuit of liberty, independence, and free will for all members of the Cainite race. Tomorrow, you shall have our rebuttal.\u201d<br /> <br /> The following day, BNP Paribas, a prominent French banking concern, informed three hedge funds that they would not be permitted to withdraw funds due to \u201ca complete evaporation of liquidity.\u201d Other banks followed, quickly triggering a panic among investors in Europe and the United States. By September of 2008, most of the Western world was in the grip of the Great Recession, the worst global financial crisis since the end of the Great Depression in the 1930\u2019s.<br /> <br /> To the kine, the Great Recession was the foreseeable result of greed, lack of regulation, and human stupidity. The Camarilla knows better. Its investigation shows that the crash, which risked totally collapsing most Western economies, was somehow engineered by the Red Question. Many of the banks that collapsed due to lack of liquidity were actually victims of computer hacking intended to manipulate each bank\u2019s ledgers and asset sheets so as to hide how overextended the bank was. Furthermore, many of the bank officials themselves show signs of having been mentally influenced into making their most disastrous financial decisions.<br /> The Camarilla investigators believe that the Red Question must have spent years prepping for the financial panic they triggered, but to the elder Camarilla leaders who are largely ignorant of the processes involved, it appears as though the Red Question simply flipped a switch and incinerated most of their stock portfolios. </div> </div> </div>So as Syndicate says: war with the vampire is unprofitable.<br /> You'd had to play it on a not so solid ground (the financial market), against people who have ammassed as much money as you have even more you should do it while you are politically weak, because the NWO is keeping its eyes on you, waiting for a casus belli.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's way more profitable to do buisness with them.<br /> <br /> Remember that the Syndicate doesn't have moral concern regarding this, they are free traders, for a free-market, they do not believe in the rules and limits of NWO, so if it is profitable trading with vampires then let's trade with vampires, why engage in a costly war when you can have a mutual partnership to skyrockets your mutual profits?<br /> <br /> Besides, Syndicate even respect Vampires, they really don't dislike them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires<br /> Vampires are interesting case studies. On one hand, they represent functioning anachronism in a microcosm: their secret society is based on feudalism, while they interact with our modern economy. It\u2019s a stable system, one that makes dealing with vampires relatively easy as long as their \u201cMasquerade\u201d is not threatened.<br /> <b>On the other hand, some of their longer-lived ilk have entrenched themselves in Consensual economy. Honestly, it\u2019s hard not to respect the power that comes from being able to invest in an institution for decades or even centuries \u2014 though don\u2019t mistake that respect for vampiric reverence overall. </b><br /> <br /> With those Reality Deviants, we can strike peaceful accords. Money is, after all, the lingua franca of society, and even vampires can value peace and profitable business. With the younger or more rebellious of their kind, though, that\u2019s best left to other Conventions to exterminate. Not that we can\u2019t, but our Enforcers are better served protecting the Bottom Line, and there are a bunch of overzealous Progenitors who would be happy to slaughter brutish leeches. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:14:38-07:00","id":969366,"title":"","content":"It is rather doubtful that the Giovanni really caused the Greek Financial Crisis. It is merely one of many rumors, and there are quite a lot of Vampire Necromancers carousing around. It is the Mage setting, not the Vampire one, and in any case Giovanni do not have necessary power and influence required to bankrupt a nation. Moreover, even if they are capable of causing nation-wide Economic Collapse, ruining Greek - and it is still one of the major nations - financially will not do any good for them. On the contrary, it will hurts them tremendously and postpone their grand plan even further, and Greek Vampires will never forgive them, let alone acquiesce such ruinous malfeasance. Last but not least, you need to separate Mage and Vampire setting. In the Mage, 2008 crisis was solely caused by the Global Market Correction Effect, and it broke out almost instantaneously, while in the Vampire it is ultimate fruition of long time machinations of the Red Question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-14-2016, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:15:14-07:00","id":969412,"title":"","content":"The Mage setting is the Vampire setting. Repeat after me, there is only one World of Darkness. The Vampires of VtM are the same as the Vampires of MtAs, it is just that Mages do not know that much about them and, mistakenly, do not think that they are a major threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:21:07-07:00","id":969415,"title":"","content":"Besides is the inevitable destiny of the setting, with the 5th edition there will be only one world of darkness (as it is now by the way,as it is officially since the week of nightmares, but with the 5th edition this whole charade of &quot;it's not the same setting!&quot; will be thrown into oblivion forever).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-14-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:21:39-07:00","id":969577,"title":"","content":"Now, the question is what will be the foundational cosmology. I hope it is the Fera cosmology, since it is the most detailed, the most internally consistent, and because the Changing Breeds predate every other splat by 250 million years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:47:32-07:00","id":969587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969577#post969577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the question is what will be the foundational cosmology. I hope it is the Fera cosmology, since it is the most detailed, the most internally consistent, and because the Changing Breeds predate every other splat by 250 million years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking just one game's cosmology and saying that the others are all wrong would be just taking a giant crap on all of the players of the other game lines. A really terrible idea both for PR and for the themes that are represented in each game.<br /> <br /> If, for some bizarre reason, they decide to make one cosmology the right one, it should probably be Mage cosmology as it is capable of incorporating the other cosmologies better than any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:49:37-07:00","id":969635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969412#post969412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage setting is the Vampire setting. Repeat after me, there is only one World of Darkness. The Vampires of VtM are the same as the Vampires of MtAs, it is just that Mages do not know that much about them and, mistakenly, do not think that they are a major threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I disagree. It is NOT. And if it is indeed oWoD, we call it internal inconsistency. Repeat after me; there is as many as World of Darkness the Players deem &quot;right&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;, &quot;convenient&quot;, &quot;necessary&quot;, &quot;preferable&quot;, or &quot;IMO&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-15-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:45:12-07:00","id":969676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969587#post969587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taking just one game's cosmology and saying that the others are all wrong would be just taking a giant crap on all of the players of the other game lines. A really terrible idea both for PR and for the themes that are represented in each game.<br /> <br /> If, for some bizarre reason, they decide to make one cosmology the right one, it should probably be Mage cosmology as it is capable of incorporating the other cosmologies better than any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? It completely contradicts the cosmological of Changelings, Fera, and Kuei-jin. In Mage, humans are the center of the Universe. In every other gameline, humans are not the center of the Universe, they are annoyances or prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:33:18-07:00","id":969726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969676#post969676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? It completely contradicts the cosmological of Changelings, Fera, and Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in turnabout, those contradict each other, as well as them contradicting Mage. That's the point. That's the *problem* when it comes to tieing everything together. It doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Mage, humans are the center of the Universe. In every other gameline, humans are not the center of the Universe, they are annoyances or prey. </div> </div> </div>And it also makes up the core mood, philosophy and style of the game. Crossover is not the default WoD Modus Operandi.<br /> So Brother's statement stands: No matter which gameline you pick as the dominant one when doing crossover, you are shafting another's fluff and mood, at least in parts. And that is fine.<br /> <br /> What isn't fine is suddenly demanding that one of the gamelines is 'right and true' for everybody, no matter what they preferred before.<br /> Which is also why I highly doubt this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969415#post969415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides is the inevitable destiny of the setting, with the 5th edition there will be only one world of darkness (as it is now by the way,as it is officially since the week of nightmares, but with the 5th edition this whole charade of &quot;it's not the same setting!&quot; will be thrown into oblivion forever).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's *possible*, but I highly doubt it. it will not suddenly unify all the contradicting origins and themes.<br /> One World of Darkness seems to be more about having the same specific WoD lores in all media (And the new WW seems to be all about spreading WoD in as many media as possible). So in a Vampire television series, you will get the WoD Vampire lore. No deviations, no 'inspired by' or 'based on'. In a Mage Novel, you will get the whole Mage mood shebang. in a Werewolf Movie, the writers will stick to the WtA lore instead of simply taking leeway and liberties. And the stories in those media flow right back into the core WoD.<br /> That's what One World Of Darkness seems to be about.<br /> <br /> But you cannot unify all the lore of all settings and not shaft one of the gamelines as written, hard.<br /> <br /> Case in point, even Chronicles Of Darkness, which is touted as being much more coherent and unified, basically keeps that unification to having a central rulebook with all the mechanics that are common between the splats and basic mood set for the World Of Darkness in general. And, well, more fleshed out mechanics.<br /> <br /> Beyond that you get the same old contradictions again, with things like the God-Machine (Oh how I love the God-machine!) not meshing with the Exarchs, Abyss and Supernal World of Awakening, etc.<br /> <br /> I doubt One World of Darkness is striving to do better. It's, as I said, more about having coherence between different media. What they *are* planning on doing is making the big metaplot more player-centric, which kind of also lessens some of the problems, as huge, global things that contradict between gamelines might pop up less.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> P.s. that said, I love CofD's Lovecraftian feel and horror. CWoD has become such a bland, non-horror Superheroesque Splat Brawl in parts. See: Threads like these.<br /> Or heck, try to have mortal or mortal-esque characters meet a weird mystery in CWoD without the players going 'oh, it's a X'.<br /> CWoD needs a big dash of 'There is more than the games presented' primers and suggestions. Another reason not to unify and melt down stuff to a common denominator.<br /> If there ever is a unification of the WoD origins, none of the previous cosmologies and origin stories should be correct. None. It's what characters might believe, but all of them, all of it should actually be wrong, and the truth should be a mystery. That's the only way to handle it fairly between all splats and settings. And it might make things suspenseful and strange again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-15-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:22:51-07:00","id":969748,"title":"","content":"There is no handling fairly. 5th will have to create one central cosmology and explain how each splat interprets it if there is a unified world of darkness (otherwise, it will just create the same mess as cWoD). That alone implies an objective reality, which also implies that the subjectivity of Mage will be incorrect. <br /> <br /> It would be realitively easy to square the circle with Mages. The subjectivity of Mages will probably be explained as a product of their Avatars filtering their perceptions so they do not have to acknowledge minor violations of their paradigms. In effect, it will finally be acknowledged that all Mages are as mad as a hatter until they Ascend, that their madness is an integral part of achieving Ascension, though the Marauders do it with style. The Consensus will be just a comforting lie that Mages tell each other because it fits better within their subjective realities than the idea that there are forces beyond that controllable by any Mage shaping reality. Ascension could even be achieving union with one of those forces.<br /> <br /> You also would not need to do much for Vampire. You would tell the legends of their Creation and, other than that, let the ST decide whether the God that cursed them was something outside of the cosmology (a universal rather than a local force) or if was a local force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T02:14:55-07:00","id":969774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969748#post969748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no handling fairly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> You can't, unless you do the opposite, and *don't* specify The Truth.<br /> Or: You state one that invalidates *all* previous gamelines' origin lores.<br /> And at that point I have to ask 'Is that really worth it? Really? You might as well just treat it as separate from CWoD.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5th will have to create one central cosmology and explain how each splat interprets it if there is a unified world of darkness (otherwise, it will just create the same mess as cWoD). That alone implies an objective reality, which also implies that the subjectivity of Mage will be incorrect. </div> </div> </div>And pretty much wreck the game's theme-as-written.<br /> &quot;That's what I always wanted to happen! Gamelines I don't even use changing everything, because unification!&quot; said no non-crossover tabletopper ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also would not need to do much for Vampire. You would tell the legends of their Creation and, other than that, let the ST decide whether the God that cursed them was something outside of the cosmology (a universal rather than a local force) or if was a local force. </div> </div> </div>So basically your solution is 'Mage is wrong, Vampire shouldn't matter and be up to the ST'.<br /> Color me absolutely not suprised. All you left out is 'Hint, Werewolf cosmology should be it'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T03:08:03-07:00","id":969787,"title":"","content":"No guys it's cool I've got this.<br /> <br /> <i>All possible hypothetical cosmologies</i> are true somewhere in the depths of the All-Set.<br /> <br /> There, consistency achieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T03:10:15-07:00","id":969789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969787#post969787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No guys it's cool I've got this.<br /> <br /> <i>All possible hypothetical cosmologies</i> are true somewhere in the depths of the All-Set.<br /> <br /> There, consistency achieved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, technically the Tellurian is endless, so..kind of?<br /> Wait. Wait, are you saying that the solution to the problem is a<br /> *shades*<br /> Quantum-boost?<br /> <br /> ..don't hurt me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:00:13-07:00","id":969874,"title":"","content":"Christ - how many Mage vs. Vampire threads do we need?<br /> <br /> The primary goal of Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, and every other WoD/CoD game is to be <b>fun to play</b>. They all use some version of our real world, so it makes those games more fun if they assume actual real-world events are caused by major players in their game. So it's totally fine for a Vampire game to decide that the Giovanni were behind the Greek financial collapse, and for a Mage game to decide it was an enterprising Syndicate VPO who ate too much Paradox with his hypereconomic experiment. Those choices make those games more interesting.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really pay to try to answer all these questions with an optimal answer for all the splats. You end up with Week of Nightmares stuff, where everyone starts playing together with Technocratic space mirrors and Antediluvians and bodhisattvas and everything. That combo cosmology stuff walks a tightrope - at best it is kind of okay, and at worst we end up with 5000 forum threads about who can kill an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a crossover game, it is <b>up to you</b> to decide what parts of Mage cosmology to use and what parts of Vampire cosmology to use. The games are similar enough to make it somewhat easy, and you can use the good combo bits to help, but they are local choices for your local game. <br /> <br /> To answer the initial question - the Syndicate doesn't care who has the money, they care that they care about having money - that it's perceived as having value. The Syndicate wants profitable trade; it doesn't need to own every dollar in the world. The Syndicate is much more worried about hippies who share their worldly possessions freely and say that &quot;you can't <i>own property</i>, man.&quot; That attacks their worldview much more than any Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:26:12-07:00","id":969884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969874#post969874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary goal of Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, and every other WoD/CoD game is to be <b>fun to play</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am hitting the like button SO HARD on this whole post. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:52:23-07:00","id":969905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969874#post969874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christ - how many Mage vs. Vampire threads do we need?<br /> <br /> The primary goal of Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, and every other WoD/CoD game is to be <b>fun to play</b>. They all use some version of our real world, so it makes those games more fun if they assume actual real-world events are caused by major players in their game. So it's totally fine for a Vampire game to decide that the Giovanni were behind the Greek financial collapse, and for a Mage game to decide it was an enterprising Syndicate VPO who ate too much Paradox with his hypereconomic experiment. Those choices make those games more interesting.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really pay to try to answer all these questions with an optimal answer for all the splats. You end up with Week of Nightmares stuff, where everyone starts playing together with Technocratic space mirrors and Antediluvians and bodhisattvas and everything. That combo cosmology stuff walks a tightrope - at best it is kind of okay, and at worst we end up with 5000 forum threads about who can kill an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a crossover game, it is <b>up to you</b> to decide what parts of Mage cosmology to use and what parts of Vampire cosmology to use. The games are similar enough to make it somewhat easy, and you can use the good combo bits to help, but they are local choices for your local game.<br /> <br /> To answer the initial question - the Syndicate doesn't care who has the money, they care that they care about having money - that it's perceived as having value. The Syndicate wants profitable trade; it doesn't need to own every dollar in the world. The Syndicate is much more worried about hippies who share their worldly possessions freely and say that &quot;you can't <i>own property</i>, man.&quot; That attacks their worldview much more than any Giovanni.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur on the whole.<br /> <br /> Just a nitpick - the Syndicate will scour Giovanni from face of the Earth anyway if they are ever aware of their existence due to goal of their Endgame, even if the Syndicate does not overly concern about their abominable, a little bit too Wyrm-ish conducts and practices, though post-Anomaly Syndics will surely pay judicious attention on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-15-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:55:46-07:00","id":969957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969905#post969905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I concur on the whole.<br /> <br /> Just a nitpick - the Syndicate will scour Giovanni from face of the Earth anyway if they are ever aware of their existence due to goal of their Endgame, even if the Syndicate does not overly concern about their abominable, a little bit too Wyrm-ish conducts and practices, though post-Anomaly Syndics will surely pay judicious attention on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe. I'd say that the Union as a whole could decide that the Giovanni are a liability and that cost/benefit projections support allocating X amount of resources to degrade/destroy them. Amalgams would be formed to accomplish this directive, and along with ItX hardware and NWO coordination (and presumably some VE support for the Low Umbra), they would be funded by the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate wants everyone to believe in money and for their money to buy a comfortable life. That goal is not necessarily opposed to the existence of crazy rich oligarchs, and aside from the eventual Technocratic endgame of getting rid of all Reality Deviants, whether that oligarch is under vampiric control is not that interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:40:08-07:00","id":969989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969957#post969957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe. I'd say that the Union as a whole could decide that the Giovanni are a liability and that cost/benefit projections support allocating X amount of resources to degrade/destroy them. Amalgams would be formed to accomplish this directive, and along with ItX hardware and NWO coordination (and presumably some VE support for the Low Umbra), they would be funded by the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate wants everyone to believe in money and for their money to buy a comfortable life. That goal is not necessarily opposed to the existence of crazy rich oligarchs, and aside from the eventual Technocratic endgame of getting rid of all Reality Deviants, whether that oligarch is under vampiric control is not that interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what I mean is, the Giovanni's Endgame. Not the Union's. The Giovanni accrue wealth and power to bring the literary Hell on Earth. And that is complete inverse of the Syndicate's goal. And purgation of the Giovanni taint would be accomplished through ruining Giovanni financially, bankrupt their families, takeover/destroy their businesses and assassinate some of the key personnel, including the Giovanni himself. And these could be done by the Syndicate alone, without any other outside assistance. The Union does not need to obliterate and hunt down every last single spawns of Giovanni across the world.<br /> <br /> In short, the Syndicate solos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:01:07-07:00","id":970004,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the Syndicate could solo the Giovanni so easily. Trying to ruin them financially would likely cause as much problems for the Syndicate as for the Giovanni and the Giovanni would likely be able to reestablish their wealth relatively quickly. The Giovanni have access to ghosts which would be incredibly difficult for the Syndicate to deal with and would allow the Giovanni to gain information on the Syndicate and attack them in a variety of ways. The Syndicate could assassinate some Giovanni vampires but I assume by &quot;the Giovanni himself&quot; you meant Augustus - I don't know if the Syndicate could kill him. Assassinations would likely cause reprisals and it only takes one Syndicate Mage to be captured by the Giovanni and Dominated/Blood Bond to open up all of the Syndicate secrets to the Giovanni and give them access to a servant with true magic. I don't even think that the rest of the Technocracy would let the Syndicate take on a major foe like the Giovanni alone, it would be like a single US state declaring war on a major foreign nation.<br /> <br /> Now, if they are sure that the Giovanni and going to destroy the shroud between life and death, then yes it may be worth the risk and would certainly justify getting the rest of the Technocracy (and maybe even the Camarilla) on board with taking down the Giovanni. But unless the Syndicate see that as an immediate possibility, they are unlikely to go to war alone against such a powerful foe. It just wouldn't be profitable.<br /> <br /> Of course, as haldir says, the game is about having fun and if you want to have the Syndicate take down the Giovanni in your game, have at it. Though I think that it would make more sense given the respective nature of each group and would likely be more fun as well if (given the Syndicate and Giovanni fight) that it was a more even and drawn out battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-15-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:26:05-07:00","id":970018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=970004#post970004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the Syndicate could solo the Giovanni so easily. Trying to ruin them financially would likely cause as much problems for the Syndicate as for the Giovanni and the Giovanni would likely be able to reestablish their wealth relatively quickly. The Giovanni have access to ghosts which would be incredibly difficult for the Syndicate to deal with and would allow the Giovanni to gain information on the Syndicate and attack them in a variety of ways. The Syndicate could assassinate some Giovanni vampires but I assume by &quot;the Giovanni himself&quot; you meant Augustus - I don't know if the Syndicate could kill him. Assassinations would likely cause reprisals and it only takes one Syndicate Mage to be captured by the Giovanni and Dominated/Blood Bond to open up all of the Syndicate secrets to the Giovanni and give them access to a servant with true magic. I don't even think that the rest of the Technocracy would let the Syndicate take on a major foe like the Giovanni alone, it would be like a single US state declaring war on a major foreign nation.<br /> <br /> Now, if they are sure that the Giovanni and going to destroy the shroud between life and death, then yes it may be worth the risk and would certainly justify getting the rest of the Technocracy (and maybe even the Camarilla) on board with taking down the Giovanni. But unless the Syndicate see that as an immediate possibility, they are unlikely to go to war alone against such a powerful foe. It just wouldn't be profitable.<br /> <br /> Of course, as haldir says, the game is about having fun and if you want to have the Syndicate take down the Giovanni in your game, have at it. Though I think that it would make more sense given the respective nature of each group and would likely be more fun as well if (given the Syndicate and Giovanni fight) that it was a more even and drawn out battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>How the Giovanni could reestablish their thousands-year-accumulated wealth quickly? Via generous usage of Domination, perhaps? And post-Anomaly Syndicate has their own secret Spirit division, namely Special Information Security Division. One of its primary task is finding, investigating and analyzing SPD products through Dimensional Science. Thus I think the Syndicate could counter Ghosts with relative ease.<br /> <br /> As for the reprisals, the reverse is also true. The Syndicate could capture any Giovanni Vampire and interrogate it with Mind magick many of their numbers are so well-versed at and exhume valuable information and secrets. Oh, and they could brainwash the Vampire, also, and use it as spies, informants and deep-cover agents.<br /> <br /> And to dispatch the August himself, the Syndicate could reliably send a bunch of Masters of Force, who the Syndicate has aplenty.<br /> <br /> Finally, remember even a single US state is able to beat a lesser nation with relative ease. But it seems you are assuming the Giovanni could go toe-to-toe against the Camarilla and the Technocracy, both are arguably the biggest and the mightiest power players in the setting. I have always thought the Giovanni is one of the lesser players, and only managed to survive thanks to cunning exploitation of incessant conflicts between the Camarilla and the Sabbat, two of the major players. But we are all aware of the fact that if only a fifth of US military assault the Maxico, the outcome is already predestined.<br /> <br /> In any case, I think the outcome could be differ whether it is the Mage-centric setting or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-15-2016, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:34:19-07:00","id":970235,"title":"","content":"Erm, the Giovanni's endgame is Void Engineer territory. Like, the Conventions and Methodologies have actual specific remits and jurisdictions that they're in charge of, that's part of the whole internal politicking the Union does behind the monolithic facade.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the NSC would like Enforcer support if they ever end up going against the Giovanni, at the very least for tracing their holdings, but it's really not the Syndicate's ballpark as an organization. Ensuring the integrity of the Shroud and Gauntlet are firmly in the NSC's court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:04:32-07:00","id":970900,"title":"","content":"I think that the Syndicate could also turn over any proof of Giovanni End Game to the Camarilla. The Camarilla could solo the Giovanni and, if they became aware that the Giovanni were trying to destroy the world, they would have sufficient motivation. I think that the Milliners would quickly abandon the Giovanni in the scenario (coincidentally taking all of the Giovanni's US holdings with them) and help the Camarilla hunt down the Giovanni proper in the USA and Canada (the Milliners are well known for keeping grudges and sixty years of being treating like trash by the Giovanni has created a lot of grudges on the part of the Milliners). The Harbingers of Skulls would effectively prevent the Giovanni from being able to join the Sabbat, so they would have nowhere to run and nowhere to hide. <br /> <br /> In that scenario, the Syndicate could just sit back and snatch up any Giovanni that the Camarilla managed to miss, which would greatly reduce the amount of resources that the Syndicate has to spend to deal with the Giovanni. In fact, the Syndicate might be able to make a profit, as the Camarilla would likely not be able to find all of the hidden assets of the Giovanni before the Syndicate found them. In the end, I would estimate that 1% of the total revenue of the global economy would be up for grabs, so we are talking about investments that generate $780 billion (nominal) per year of earnings. If the Milliners joined the Camarilla, the Camarilla would probably be able to grab investments that generate $390 billion (nominal) per year of earnings, which would leave investments that generated $390 billion (nominal) up for grabs. I imagine that the Syndicate would be very interested in grabbing as much of those investments as possible, though I imagine that there would be plenty for everyone, so there would be plenty of supernaturals feeding off of the corpse of the Giovanni Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:33:08-07:00","id":971569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=969577#post969577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the question is what will be the foundational cosmology. I hope it is the Fera cosmology, since it is the most detailed, the most internally consistent, and because the Changing Breeds predate every other splat by 250 million years.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read Masters of the Art, there are very strong implications that the universe and it's inhabitants, including the Umbra and all it's denizens, were created by a Prime Oracle from another universe.<br /> <br /> Mage cosmology therefor predates the existence of reality.<br /> <br /> This also explains why certain things work the way they do. Why is Time Travel Double-Plus Ungood? Because the creator said fuck that and made it so. All the 'Earthly Foundations.' Aren't random Arbitrary rules that exist for no apparent reason. They're the backbone of the Tellurian as crafted by the Creator the ludicrously powerful mage from a higher dimension.<br /> <br /> Taking this view, and then using the Iterator explanation for the other supernaturals as the product of either the traditions or magic groups even predating the traditions. Much as the Technocracy has slid guns and cars into the consensus. The greater spirits would be crafted by the Creator-Mage and then would spawn their lesser kin.<br /> <br /> Why do vampires exist? Because the Creator-Mage said &quot;FUCK YOU.&quot; to caine and in a moment of stupidity, granted him supernatural powers, immortality, and a raging hunger for human blood. Because just because you're a transcendantly powerful mage doesn't mean you can't be an idiot.<br /> <br /> Mage cosmology makes so much more sense as a dominant cosmology than the others since it essentially says &quot;Anything is Possible.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:43:41-07:00","id":971573,"title":"","content":"Which is just an excuse for laziness and inconsistencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:04:27-07:00","id":971589,"title":"","content":"So essentially your argument is that we should fuck over literally every game line except Werewolf. Because to do otherwise is to be lazy. Even when there is an existing game line who's existing cosmology can neatly contain the others independent cosmologies with minimal disruptions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:40:11-07:00","id":971603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971589#post971589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So essentially your argument is that we should fuck over literally every game line except Werewolf. Because to do otherwise is to be lazy. Even when there is an existing game line who's existing cosmology can neatly contain the others independent cosmologies with minimal disruptions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Mage is original flavor 7th Sea-ing the entire setup, to be honest. Or perhaps being more like Exalted 2nd edition than Exalted 2nd edition was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:57:47-07:00","id":971614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971589#post971589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So essentially your argument is that we should fuck over literally every game line except Werewolf. Because to do otherwise is to be lazy. Even when there is an existing game line who's existing cosmology can neatly contain the others independent cosmologies with minimal disruptions?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a Flying Spaghetti Monster argument. Whether you are using a bearded man, a flying spaghetti monster, or a sapient lasagna, it still suffers from the same fallacy, a fallacy that is based on an unwillingness to accept that human beliefs are nothing to reality. Humans are only important to humans, the Earth existed for over four billion years before humans evolved and it will likely exist for over four billion years after humans go extinct. Mages, in their arrogance and their hubris, cannot accept that they are inconsequential to reality, so they create their own myths that support their relevance. Instead of the Consensus just shaping magic, they claim that the Consensus shapes reality (which is really like how small children occasionally refuse to believe that anything outside of their experience exists because it conflicts with their own unconscious narrative).<br /> <br /> Of course, the reason why the Mage books support the Mage cosmology is that they are written from the Tradition perspective (just like Vampire is written from the Kindred perspective and Werewolf is written from the Garou perspective). The style of White Wolf during the 90's was to always support the subjective position of the supernatural creatures that they were focused on, regardless of how odd their beliefs may otherwise be, because White Wolf liked giving their creations voice. The adventures were also written from the same subjective position because White Wolf was always fair in that way.<br /> <br /> My preference for the Garou perspective over that of the Mage perspective and the Vampire perspective comes from the simple fact that it contradicts science less than the other two perspectives. While many things about the Garou perspective are not terribly scientific, at least it acknowledges the basics of astronomy, evolution, plate tectonics, etc. The perspectives of the other major supernatural creatures do not even acknowledge even those simple and straightforward ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:27:41-07:00","id":971636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971614#post971614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a Flying Spaghetti Monster argument. Whether you are using a bearded man, a flying spaghetti monster, or a sapient lasagna, it still suffers from the same fallacy, a fallacy that is based on an unwillingness to accept that human beliefs are nothing to reality. Humans are only important to humans, the Earth existed for over four billion years before humans evolved and it will likely exist for over four billion years after humans go extinct. Mages, in their arrogance and their hubris, cannot accept that they are inconsequential to reality, so they create their own myths that support their relevance. Instead of the Consensus just shaping magic, they claim that the Consensus shapes reality (which is really like how small children occasionally refuse to believe that anything outside of their experience exists because it conflicts with their own unconscious narrative).<br /> <br /> Of course, the reason why the Mage books support the Mage cosmology is that they are written from the Tradition perspective (just like Vampire is written from the Kindred perspective and Werewolf is written from the Garou perspective). The style of White Wolf during the 90's was to always support the subjective position of the supernatural creatures that they were focused on, regardless of how odd their beliefs may otherwise be, because White Wolf liked giving their creations voice. The adventures were also written from the same subjective position because White Wolf was always fair in that way.<br /> <br /> My preference for the Garou perspective over that of the Mage perspective and the Vampire perspective comes from the simple fact that it contradicts science less than the other two perspectives. While many things about the Garou perspective are not terribly scientific, at least it acknowledges the basics of astronomy, evolution, plate tectonics, etc. The perspectives of the other major supernatural creatures do not even acknowledge even those simple and straightforward ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy says hello. You know. The faction that will <i>literally murder people for not believing in science.</i><br /> <br /> Edit: And actually I need to say more to this.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is more scientific than Vampire or Mage? Mage posits that there are deeper laws to reality than those written by science and that by tapping into those laws one can create effects. Plate Tectonics, Evolution, and the laws of physics ACTUALLY EXIST in mage. They might be largely written by the Technocracy, but they are still concrete things that exist much as they do in real life.<br /> <br /> And Vampire literally posits no change to IRL reality except to say that &quot;God is real, he really cursed Caine and spawned a race of undead abominations with weird powers that drink blood. These undead now form an illuminati esque group to control the world. Science is LITERALLY exactly the same as it is in the real world. Only with magic. Less magic in fact than is entailed in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Werewolfs entire cosmology is literally &quot;The spirits did it.&quot; I'm not even joking. White Supremacy? Spirits did it. Highways? Spirits did it. It's raining outside? The Spirits did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:45:59-07:00","id":971648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971636#post971636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy says hello. You know. The faction that will <i>literally murder people for not believing in science.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>As a whole, Mage has some serious problems with what timeline it's using, and the presence of the Technocracy doesn't help. With Werewolf, you know that the Earth is as old as the scientific method has uncovered, as far the physical side goes, and it's not subject to any effectual argument based on belief. Also, the cosmos being vast and uncaring about humans, with frightening beings waiting in the wings? Isn't much of that exactly what the Technocracy uses to sell their views?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:56:58-07:00","id":971658,"title":"","content":"And the Traditions do not do the same to the people who endanger their Consensus? There are no 'white hats' in Mage, there are just lunatics who failed to Ascend who range from 'gray hat' to 'black hat'. That is the entire point of Mage, in fact, the disappointment and the insanity that comes from failing to give up power so that you can Ascend, the grasping desire to have your cake and eat it too. <br /> <br /> That is why I like the game, as the condition of Mages are literally the most tragic of all the supernatural creatures in the cWoD, because they are failures who have taken power (Arete or Enlightenment from the Mage perspective) over Ascension (Nirvana from the Buddhist perspective). Every Mage in existence has failed at least once, and probably more than once, to choose Ascension and, instead, chose power. Now, they may have good moral reasons for their choice ('I have to take care of my children', 'I have to finish a cure for cancer', or 'I am in love'), but they will almost inevitably continue to choose power over Ascension because power because the reason for their existence. <br /> <br /> The greatest tragedy of course, is that they think that they can gain Ascension as well as power if they cheat, by 'furthering' the Ascension of all of humanity, which would ironically mean the mass extinction of humanity. Whether they belong to the Technocracy or the Traditions, the Marauders or the Nephandi, they are all afflicted by the same tragedy that unifies all Mages. It is strangely appropriate that Mage attracts the type of players who would choose power over Ascension. <br /> <br /> When I would run my Mage games back in the 90s and 00s, I would give my players a choice with every successful seeking. On one hand, they could choose to Ascend and, in the process of Ascension, cause one small change to occur in the world of their choice (the equivalent of a level 5 Numina effect with 15 automatic successes, representing the energy released by the sacrifice of their humanity). In addition, I would allow them to create an equivalent character, with experience points equal to the amount that they earned, who they could introduce in the next session, though they would have a minimum of four sessions before they could have another chance at a seeking. On the other hand, they could choose to purchase a dot of Arete. Not one of my players ever took the first option, ever, because they unconsciously desired power for their character more than they desired Ascension for their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:08:42-07:00","id":971666,"title":"","content":"The Traditions don't HAVE a consensus.<br /> <br /> This is your headcanon. This is not how Mage is actually meant to work.<br /> <br /> Mage is not a Tragic game. It's an inherently optimistic game. Mages are not Tragic Figures as a whole.<br /> <br /> And what 'Ascension' means depends upon the faction in question. It's an ephemeral ideal. Not one specific thing. For the Iterators, it's the creation of a perfectly ordered universe that runs like clockwork. &quot;Predictability equals Perfection, and thus Ascension.&quot; When the world has become predictable in all things, the world will have ascended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:19:37-07:00","id":971771,"title":"","content":"The Traditions are not trying to change the Consensus? They are not promoting an anti-science Consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:14:51-07:00","id":971821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971771#post971771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions are not trying to change the Consensus? They are not promoting an anti-science Consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and no, respectively.<br /> <br /> &quot;Consensus&quot; isn't a buzzword for &quot;how reality is at the moment&quot;. It's called that because it's a result of humanity the world over agreeing, in general, what the world is like on a basic level. The Technocracy wants a Consensus; they're the force of conformity trying to make the world work, on a basic level, the same way everywhere.<br /> <br /> The Traditions don't <i>want</i> that. They want dissent, not consensus. Magically as well as politically.<br /> <br /> Well, insofar as the Traditions as a whole can be said to &quot;want&quot; anything. The Conventions may be politically divided, but they at least agree on the basic nature of existence on some level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:33:15-07:00","id":971830,"title":"","content":"Also, Science is not the enemy of Magick or Faith. Sir Isaac Newton wrote extensively on all three topics. And there are plenty of groups within the Traditions that incorporate or espouse some form of Scientific or Technological thought. Not just the two technomancer Traditions, either, but a multitude of technomancers within normally mystic groups. Just taking one example, the Alexandrian Society, in the Celestial Chorus, are fully on board with Science. They just want to reconcile it with the existence of a Creator.<br /> <br /> The reason the Traditions oppose the Technocracy is because the Technocratic Union works towards an autocratic agenda. The Technos would have the world dancing to the beat of one drum - the drum the Union controls. That drum just happens to be Science, but it could be anything if the Union thought it could control humanity. The Syndicate, for instance, would use nothing but Economics to control the world if it really needed to. If Magick became a known quantity in the world, the Syndicate would be looking for ways to monetize it (and, through the function of markets and supply/demand, control it).<br /> <br /> I'm 100% positive there was a sidebar in M20 - fairly early in the core book - that explained this very thing. That Science wasn't the enemy - authoritarian elitists were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:08:56-07:00","id":971898,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy wants an orderly, reliable universe while the Traditions want the universe to contain multitudes of possibilities and potential. Consistency versus inconsistency. Having running water in every house conflicts with having a pet water elemental.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971658#post971658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I would run my Mage games back in the 90s and 00s, I would give my players a choice with every successful seeking. On one hand, they could choose to Ascend and, in the process of Ascension, cause one small change to occur in the world of their choice (the equivalent of a level 5 Numina effect with 15 automatic successes, representing the energy released by the sacrifice of their humanity). In addition, I would allow them to create an equivalent character, with experience points equal to the amount that they earned, who they could introduce in the next session, though they would have a minimum of four sessions before they could have another chance at a seeking. On the other hand, they could choose to purchase a dot of Arete. Not one of my players ever took the first option, ever, because they unconsciously desired power for their character more than they desired Ascension for their character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe they liked their character and weren't done with them yet. Ascension presumes they can't play that character any more. It can be a rational player choice without assuming both character and player are helplessly power-hungry. <br /> <br /> I know it's in the name of the game, but I never saw Mage as a game you &quot;won&quot; by ascending. (By contrast, I can't help but see Werewolf as a game you &quot;lose&quot; automatically in the Apocalypse.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:40:12-07:00","id":971974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968857-the-syndicate-and-the-vampire?p=971830#post971830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason the Traditions oppose the Technocracy is because the Technocratic Union works towards an autocratic agenda. The Technos would have the world dancing to the beat of one drum - the drum the Union controls. That drum just happens to be Science, but it could be anything if the Union thought it could control humanity. (...)<br /> The Syndicate, for instance, would use nothing but Economics to control the world if it really needed to. If Magick became a known quantity in the world, the Syndicate would be looking for ways to monetize it (and, through the function of markets and supply/demand, control it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Technocracy, since it's creation as the Order of Reason, actually there to guide and protect humanity using science and reason, because the alternatives are deemed to be too unstable, dangerous and unreliable?<br /> In practice it means abandoning the exploration of Umbra (except through the scientific Dimensional Science Paradigm, which in practice kills off or changes parts of Umbra and it's denizens to conform to it), Sanitizing Nodes, killing Thaumivores, leaving the Wraiths to themselves and reforging True Magick capabilities of humanity into Enlightened Science. Their main goals seems to be propagation of their approach to how they see the role of the Awakened (sorry,<i> Enlightened</i>) in the world; and protection of humanity from the supernatural - both of which tend to lead towards autocratic approaches and attitudes. But control in itself does not seem to be the goal of Order of Reason/Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-18-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}